ays mid on the heater, and ends on the home view.","hold":true},"sentences":[{"role":"hook","text":"If you heat a tank of water over a flame, you have a water heater."},{"role":"problem","text":"But the heat leaks out through the thin walls, and the water cools."},{"role":"fix1","text":"So you wrap the tank in a thick foam jacket."},{"role":"problem2","text":"But now the foam traps it all, and the water keeps heating."},{"role":"fix2","text":"So you add a thermostat that shuts the flame off at 120 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"role":"name","text":"This is a water heater."},{"role":"how","text":"A dip tube carries cold water down, and hot water leaves the top."},{"role":"myth","text":"And the rod inside is not a heater."},{"role":"mythFact","text":"It is an anode rod that rusts instead of the steel tank."},{"role":"finish","text":"Add a relief valve, a flue and a drain."},{"role":"congrats","text":"Congratulations, you have built a water heater."}]}